  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: ClinCare 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "Your sister is thinking about joining a clinical trial. You attend the
    pre-trial consultation with her and take notes while the doctor explains the
    treatment plan and possible side effects.\n\n<b>Caregivers can\u2019t help patients
    decide whether to join a clinical trial\u2014that\u2019s strictly between the
    patient and doctor.</b>\n\nIs this <b>true</b> or <b>false</b>?"
  explanation: Caregivers often play a major role in helping patients understand
    trial details, weigh risks and benefits, and make informed decisions that reflect
    their personal values and comfort level. They can also help patients prepare
    questions for the research team and process complex information after appointments.
    By offering emotional reassurance and clear communication, caregivers help patients
    feel confident and supported in whatever choice they make.
  correctAnswer: False
  incorrectAnswer1: True
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Caregiver
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Clinical
